States: Standards

Purpose:
  Defines standard states for .sdd entities.

EntityStates:
  DRAFT:
    Description: Initial creation, not ready
  EXPERIMENTAL:
    Description: Being tested, may change
  STABLE:
    Description: Production-ready, stable
  DEPRECATED:
    Description: Being phased out
  RETIRED:
    Description: No longer used

TaskStates:
  DRAFT:
    Task created, not ready
  READY:
    Dependencies satisfied, ready to start
  ACTIVE:
    Currently being worked on
  BLOCKED:
    Waiting for dependency or approval
  DONE:
    Completed and verified
  FAILED:
    Execution failed
  ARCHIVED:
    No longer relevant

WorkflowStates:
  PENDING:
    Not started
  RUNNING:
    In progress
  PASSED:
    Completed successfully
  FAILED:
    Failed
  BLOCKED:
    Waiting for dependency
  SKIPPED:
    Not applicable
  WAIVED:
    Approved to skip
  EXPIRED:
    Waiver expired

GateStates:
  PENDING
  RUNNING
  PASSED
  FAILED
  BLOCKED
  SKIPPED
  WAIVED
  EXPIRED

StateRules:
  [SS1]  All entities MUST have a state.
  [SS2]  State transitions MUST follow defined flows.
  [SS3]  ARCHIVED state preserves history, does not delete.
  [SS4]  WAIVED state requires expiration date.

State: +
  